-- CK-22: D1 across three modules (checker-v2.md §11.3, D1 as amended
-- 2026-09-24; R8b's reviewer focus). `A`'s `eq` compares modulo 10 and is
-- private, so it answers only inside `A`. `B` wraps an `A.T` and compares
-- nothing: its `Wrap` has no `eq` anyone may use, and its record says so
-- (`private_method`, naming `A.T`: §14.2 *as amended by R8b*). `C` compares
-- two `B.Wrap`s: `private_method` at its `==`, and the message says which
-- private method, of which type, the value holds. On 7427828 (and on v2
-- before R8b) `C` builds: `B`'s row said "derives" (v1) or "does not
-- support" (R8a), never why.
pub type T
    = T Int


eq : T, T -> Bool
eq left right =
    case left of
        T x ->
            case right of
                T y ->
                    modBy x 10 == modBy y 10


pub inside : T, T -> Bool
inside a b =
    a == b
